  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the general business law, in relation to the hiring of\nsecurity guards by public sports venues with a capacity of at least sixty\nthousand people located in the county of Erie; and to amend a chapter of the\nlaws of 2021 amending the general business law relating to the applicability\nof the security guard act of nineteen hundred ninety-two to facilities owned\nby a public sports venue, as proposed in legislative bills numbers S. 7142-A\nand A. 7960-A, in relation to the effectiveness thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S7832",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7832-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §89-w, Gen Bus L; amd §2, Chap of 2021 (as proposed in S.7142-A & A.7960-A)",
    "lawSection": "General Business Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7832\n\nSPONSOR: KENNEDY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the general business law, in relation to the hiring of\nsecurity guards by public sports venues with a capacity of at least\nsixty thousand people located in the county of Erie; and to amend a\nchapter of the laws of 2021 amending the general business law relating\nto the applicability of the security guard act of nineteen hundred nine-\nty-two to facilities owned by a public sports venue, as proposed in\nlegislative bills numbers S. 7142-A and A. 7960-A, in relation to the\neffectiveness thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis is a chapter amendment that makes changes to a chapter of the laws\nof 2021, enacting S.7142-A/A.7960-A.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis legislation amends the underlying chapter by narrowing the scope of\nthe underlying chapter.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Executive expressed agreement with the underlying legislation but\nwanted to narrow the reach of the legislation. This Chapter Amendment is\nthe negotiated result of that request by the Executive. This Chapter\nAmendment will impose a three-year sunset period and limit the exemption\nprovided by the legislation to publicly-owned sports venues with a\ncapacity of at least 60,000 people, within the county of Erie. Anyone\nwithin the reach of the exemption will still need to employ at least 50%\nlicensed security guards.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter amendment to a chapter of the laws of 2021, enacting\nS.7142-A/A.7960-A.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately, provided, however, that section\none of this act shall take effect on the same date and in the same\nmanner as a chapter of the laws of 2021 amending the general business\nlaw relating to the applicability of the security guard act of nineteen\nhundred ninety-two to facilities owned by a public sports venue, as\nproposed in legislative bills numbers S.7142-A and A.7960-A, takes\neffect.\n",
